course: dictionary
lesson: 10807
title: Varnish: a clear, shiny protector
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Varnish is a clear liquid that you paint onto wood or other surfaces. When it dries, it makes a hard, shiny layer that protects the surface underneath.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Rat and Mole were painting and varnishing, mending paddles, repairing cushions» lists jobs you do to get things ready, so varnishing is something you do to a surface. Try your meaning in the sentence: "painting and painting a clear shiny coat" still makes sense.
explain: Varnish also means something different in «nail varnish». Here it is coloured paint for fingernails and toenails, not a clear coat for wood. Check the words next to it, like nail or clear, to know which meaning the writer means.
fact: Varnish is a clear liquid that dries to a hard, shiny, protective layer.
fact: To varnish something means to paint it with varnish.
fact: «Nail varnish» is coloured paint for fingernails and toenails; in the US it is called nail polish.
fact: Varnish has strong fumes, so use it with an adult, in a room with open windows, and wash your brushes properly.
fact: A clear varnish protects an oil painting, but it can turn yellow over time.
exercise: «Rat and Mole were painting and varnishing, mending paddles, repairing cushions.» What does varnishing mean here? | *Painting a surface with varnish | Sleeping on the riverbank | Catching fish from the river | Tying a knot in a rope
exercise: Which of these is nail varnish? | A clear liquid that makes wood shiny | A kind of wood used for paddles | A tool for mending boats | *Coloured paint for fingernails and toenails
exercise: Find and copy the word from «A clear varnish protects an oil painting» that tells you the varnish has no colour. | *clear | protects | painting | oil
test: Varnish is best described as | A soft, sticky food | *A clear liquid that dries to a hard, shiny layer | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of wood for building boats
test: Why should you use varnish with an adult, in a room with open windows? | Varnish is very cold and can freeze your hands | *Varnish has strong fumes | Varnish is a kind of soap | Varnish needs sunlight to work
exam: In «A clear varnish protects an oil painting, but it yellows over time», what job does the varnish do? | It washes the paint off the painting | It makes the painting bigger | *It protects the painting | It turns the painting into wood
